<title>HONG KONG: C.Lyonnais sets warrant on Taiwan electronic firms.</title>
<headline>C.Lyonnais sets warrant on Taiwan electronic firms.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Lyonnais Financial Products (Guernsey) Ltd said on Thursday it proposed to issue 50 million American-style call warrants on a basket of six Taiwan electronics companies.</p>
<p>Each basket comprises of:</p>
<p> Acer Inc				     0.20 shares</p>
<p> CMC Magnetics Corp			 0.15 shares</p>
<p> Compaq MFTG				  0.06 shares</p>
<p> Taiwan Semiconductor		     0.14 shares</p>
<p> United Microelectronics Corporation  0.20 shares</p>
<p> Yageo Corp				   0.15 shares</p>
<p>One warrant controls one basket.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE	NT$71.8695     PREMIUM    21.05 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	 NT$24.79	 GEARING    3.22x</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	  12 MONTHS	EXER LOT   1,000</p>
<p> LISTING	     LUXEMBOURG     PAYDATE    3 WKS AFTER LAUNCH</p>
<p> REFERENCE SPOT    NT$79.855</p>
<p> GOVERNING LAW     FRENCH</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
